"""Positive responses at reference-list boundaries.

A bare space after a comma usually introduces a number. Repeated term/number
pairs suggest a bibliography, index, or enumerated list; their recent
count increases the response, more gently around code punctuation. Other
strong patterns are relational field delimiters (notably
'instance of') and 'See also' headings. Unrecognized positions predict zero.
Only a short text tail is retained, resetting at each new document.
